Supporting evidence in the PR's own tests: `status/status_test.go:359` became

```go
if !proto.Equal(details[i].(protoreflect.ProtoMessage), tc.details[i].(protoreflect.ProtoMessage)) {
```

A cast on both operands to compare input with output is the type system reporting that the two halves of the API no longer speak the same interface. `status/status_test.go:412` also now builds its expected error with `protoimpl.X.NewError("invalid empty type URL")`; `protoimpl` is documented as being for generated code only, and pinning a test to protobuf-internal error text makes it brittle across protobuf releases. Compare on `err != nil` and type, or on `strings.Contains`, instead.

